course: dictionary
lesson: 7458
title: Words for people in charge
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A title is a special name that tells you someone's job or rank. Pope is a title. Read the words around it to find out what it means: «The Pope is the Bishop of Rome and leader of the Catholic Church worldwide.» The clues are leader, Catholic Church and worldwide, so the Pope leads a big church around the world.
explain: «Vatican City, inside Rome, is the smallest country in the world, and it is ruled by the Pope.» Ruled is another clue. Someone who rules a place is in charge of it, so the Pope is in charge of Vatican City. Try your meaning in the sentence: "it is ruled by the leader of the Catholic Church" still makes sense, so you have found it.
explain: A capital P, as in the Pope or Pope Francis, shows the title of the leader of the Catholic Church. In some Orthodox churches, pope is also a title for certain leaders, such as the Pope of Alexandria. Always check the words around the title to see which church is being talked about.
fact: The Pope is the leader of the Roman Catholic Church.
fact: The Pope lives in Vatican City, in Rome.
fact: Catholics see the Pope as following Saint Peter.
fact: Vatican City is the smallest country in the world, at about 0.44 square kilometres.
fact: In some Orthodox churches, «pope» is also a title for certain leaders, such as the Pope of Alexandria.
exercise: «The Pope is the Bishop of Rome and leader of the Catholic Church worldwide.» What is the Pope? | A king of England | A type of bird | *The leader of the Catholic Church | A football coach
exercise: Where does the Pope live? | Athens | *Vatican City, in Rome | London | Paris
exercise: Catholics see the Pope as following which saint? | *Saint Peter | Saint Patrick | Saint George | Saint Andrew
test: «Prince Danylo received a royal crown from a papal envoy (a messenger of the Pope).» What is a papal envoy? | A prince from Ukraine | A type of royal crown | A church bell | *A messenger of the Pope
test: In some Orthodox churches, what is pope? | *A title for certain leaders | A building in Rome | A school subject | A type of cloud
exam: In «The Pope leads prayers for the whole world», what does the Pope do? | He sells stamps in Vatican City | *He leads prayers for the whole world | He cooks dinner for the church | He builds castles
